            <English>Bloom duration</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashDuration_desc">
            <English>Seconds the bloom takes to fade.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashEnabled">
            <English>Muzzle flash bloom</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashEnabled_desc">
            <English>Firing without a suppressor washes the NVG image out white for a moment.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashIntensity">
            <English>Bloom intensity</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashIntensity_desc">
            <English>How white the image gets on a shot.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashNearby">
            <English>Nearby shooters</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashNearbyRange">
            <English>Nearby range</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashNearbyRange_desc">
            <English>Distance in metres within which other shooters cause bloom. Fades with distance.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashNearbyScale">
            <English>Nearby intensity</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashNearbyScale_desc">
            <English>Bloom from another shooter at point blank, relative to your own shot.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashNearby_desc">
            <English>Unsuppressed shots from other units close to you and in view also bloom your NVGs.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashRequireMagnified">
            <English>Only through magnified optics</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashRequireMagnified_desc">
            <English>Bloom only while aiming through a magnified optic.\nOff = any shot with NVGs on.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashStack">
            <English>Follow-up shot bloom</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_flashStack_desc">
            <English>Share of full bloom that a shot adds while the previous bloom is still fading (automatic fire).</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_integratedBlacklist">
            <English>Never integrated</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_integratedBlacklist_desc">
            <English>Optics never treated as integrated NV, even if auto-detection says so.\nComma separated classnames, case insensitive.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_integratedWhitelist">
            <English>Integrated NV optics</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_integratedWhitelist_desc">
            <English>Optics (or weapons with built-in optics) treated as having their own night vision: no optic features.\nComma separated classnames, case insensitive.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_keep">
            <English>Keep setting</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_magThreshold">
            <English>Magnification threshold</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_magThreshold_desc">
            <English>Zoom at or above which an optic counts as magnified. Optic features (mount failure, bruise, ADS sway,\nmisalignment, flash bloom, monocular reticle) need this. Iron sights and holo sights sit around 1.0-1.3x.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_maskEnabled">
            <English>Draw NVG tube mask</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_maskEnabled_desc">
            <English>Black out everything outside the NVG tube(s) while NVGs are on.\nOff = full screen night vision (sway then has nothing to move).</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_maskOpacity">
            <English>Mask opacity</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_maskOpacity_desc">
            <English>How dark the area outside the tubes is.\nLower = you can see a little around the tubes.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_maskScale">
            <English>Tube size</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_maskScale_desc">
            <English>Size of the tube view.\nHigher = larger tubes, less blacked out.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignAutoRecover">
            <English>Auto recover</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignAutoRecover_desc">
            <English>The mount settles back by itself after you stop shooting.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignChance">
            <English>Misalignment chance per shot</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignChance_desc">
            <English>Chance that one shot shifts the mount. Scales with the round's power.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignEnabled">
            <English>Mount misalignment</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignEnabled_desc">
            <English>Shots can shift the NVG mount so the tube sits off centre until it recovers or is re-seated. Only while aiming through a magnified optic (above the General magnification threshold) with NVGs on.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignMax">
            <English>Max misalignment</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignMax_desc">
            <English>Furthest the mount can end up off centre, as a fraction of screen height.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignRecoverDelay">
            <English>Auto recover delay</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignRecoverDelay_desc">
            <English>Seconds without firing before the mount starts settling back.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignRecoverTime">
            <English>Auto recover time</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignRecoverTime_desc">
            <English>Seconds the mount takes to settle fully back once it starts.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignStep">
            <English>Misalignment per shift</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignStep_desc">
            <English>How far one shift moves the tube, as a fraction of screen height.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignToggleReset">
            <English>NVG toggle re-seats</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_misalignToggleReset_desc">
            <English>Turning the NVGs off and on again clears the misalignment.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_monoShift">
            <English>Monocular tube shift</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_monoShift_desc">
            <English>How far a monocular tube sits off centre, as a fraction of screen width.\n0 = centred.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_monoSide">
            <English>Monocular eye</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_monoSide_desc">
            <English>Which eye a monocular NVG sits in front of. The monocular reticle appears on the other side.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_monoSide_opt0">
            <English>Left eye (reticle right)</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_monoSide_opt1">
            <English>Right eye (reticle left)</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_mountBrokenHint">
            <English>Your NVG mount broke - the goggles fell off.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_mountChance">
            <English>Failure chance per shot</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_mountChance_desc">
            <English>Chance that one shot breaks the mount.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_mountEnabled">
            <English>Mount failure</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_mountEnabled_desc">
            <English>Shots can break the NVG mount so the goggles fall to the ground. Only while aiming through a magnified optic (above the General magnification threshold) with NVGs on.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_mountNotify">
            <English>Notify player</English>
