        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reseated">
            <English>NVG mount re-seated.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reseating">
            <English>Re-seating NVG mount...</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleColor">
            <English>Reticle colour</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleColor_desc">
            <English>Colour of the reticle copy.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleColor_opt0">
            <English>Red</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleColor_opt1">
            <English>Green</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleColor_opt2">
            <English>Amber</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleColor_opt3">
            <English>Black</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleEnabled">
            <English>Monocular reticle</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleEnabled_desc">
            <English>With a monocular NVG, the naked eye still sees the scope: a copy of the reticle is drawn on the side\nwithout the tube. Only while aiming through a magnified optic (above the General magnification threshold) with NVGs on.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleMap">
            <English>Reticle per optic</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_azeroot_ronim_main_reticleMap_desc">
